  {
    "name": "MediaAsset",
    "description": "One image in the media library. Records live in the `{ assets: [] }` manifest singleton at `src/data/media.json` (the package's MEDIA_MANIFEST_PATH), which the CMS media library writes. Disk decides which assets exist \u2014 the `public/images` scan \u2014 while this record decides what is KNOWN about one, above all its alt text. `filename` is the identity: a path WITHIN `public/images`, so it may contain `/` for a nested asset (`gallery/event-05.jpg`). An explicit empty `alt` is a deliberate \"this image is decorative\", not a missing value.",
    "category": "datastore",
    "order": 12,
    "fields": [
